### **8.1 Indicative Evaluation Framework**

Proposals will be evaluated using Quality and Cost-Based Selection (QCBS). Technical proposals shall carry 80% of the total score, and financial proposals 20%. The indicative distribution of the technical score is firm-specific experience (30 points); adequacy of methodology and work plan (30 points); qualifications and competence of key experts (20 points); and knowledge transfer/participation of MARWASCO staff (10 points). The minimum technical qualifying score is 75 points. MWA reserves the right to adjust this framework in the Request for Proposals.

